{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/22091-new-guildbooks-thoughts","id":22091,"title":"New Guildbooks. Thoughts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-02T20:28:32-08:00","id":22091,"title":"New Guildbooks. Thoughts?","content":"We are missing...<br /> <br /> Guildbook: Harbingers<br /> Guildbook: Proctors<br /> Guildbook: Chanteurs<br /> Guildbook: Monitors<br /> Guildbook: Usurers<br /> <br /> The Forbidden guilds...<br /> <br /> Guildbook: Alchemists<br /> Guildbook: Solicitors<br /> <br /> Also...<br /> <br /> Guildbook: Serviteurs<br /> Guildbook: Moriman<br /> Guildbook: Tvashtriya<br /> <br /> (Though those last three seem to be pretty confined to their respective cultures so probably don't require their own guildbooks, though some folks may disagree, so I am including them anyway)<br /> <br /> In particular, I am particularly interested in the Chanteurs receiving a guildbook, because I don't think it was ever emphasized how important they could have been to wraith society, and how even though keening wasn't the <i>best </i>way of gaining pathos, it was <i>a</i> way, and thus would have made them a viable rival for the Usurers. If they do combined guildbooks again, I think the Usurers and Chanteurs should share a book for this reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T21:45:03-08:00","id":22111,"title":"","content":"Definitely interested in them.<br /> Also interested in how media (Movies, Cartoons, TV Shows, RPGs, Comics, etc.) made after W:tO ended might influence some of this as well. Because, the Proctors? That's both the NWOD Geist: The Sin-Eaters and Danny Phantom right there.<br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> I also don't buy into the myth that the Proctors have absolutely no agenda or exterior motive about crossing the shroud.<br /> And if the Hierarchy hires them to go after shroud crossers: Then you have a Wraith that can sometimes become physical/mortal that hunts down other ghosts. So yeah, you can see where I can easily make the Danny Phantom comparison there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","user":"Laughing Hyena","date":". 12-03-2013, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T22:39:27-08:00","id":22132,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.reddit.com/r/rpg/comments/1rl8vy/we_are_onyx_path_publishing_publishers_of_white/cdom4gj\" target=\"_blank\">Ian Watson's commented</a> they're more likely to do a whole new set of Guildbooks or something similar than complete the original set.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T04:00:30-08:00","id":22246,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely interested in these. Though I would also like to see the Ferrymen get their own supplement book, even just a skinny one. There's so much background and history to mine for material concerning all kinds of info on the death guides. Only in Ends of Empire do you finally get a look at what it would be like to play one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T07:51:14-08:00","id":22332,"title":"","content":"The Guilds may have come back with a vengeance since the Sixth Great Maelstrom and Charon's departure, so we definitely need new editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T09:47:15-08:00","id":22387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/22091-new-guildbooks-thoughts?p=22332#post22332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Guilds may have come back with a vengeance since the Sixth Great Maelstrom and Charon's departure, so we definitely need new editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mm. Question is whether they'll want to follow through on the metaplot - Ends of Empire being Wraith's only major metaplot book means it'd be easy to set Wr20 before it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:48:05-08:00","id":22430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/22091-new-guildbooks-thoughts?p=22387#post22387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mm. Question is whether they'll want to follow through on the metaplot - Ends of Empire being Wraith's only major metaplot book means it'd be easy to set Wr20 before it.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, and I haven't read any of the other X20 books to know how much they are or aren't following thru with metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-03T10:53:56-08:00","id":22438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/22091-new-guildbooks-thoughts?p=22387#post22387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mm. Question is whether they'll want to follow through on the metaplot - Ends of Empire being Wraith's only major metaplot book means it'd be easy to set Wr20 before it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see them going the Changing Breeds 20th's route on the Ahadi (<i>I'm a backer and was able to look at the pdf.</i>) when it comes to Wraith's metaplot. Basically, they will offer options to play before, during, or after the Sixth Great Maelstrom. As well as give plothooks for it and the issues/problems that would crop up with those events happening or not happening in your game.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T06:17:55-08:00","id":23098,"title":"","content":"I think it may be a little optimistic to expect Guildbooks for each and every Guild, as much as I would love to see them written. I do love the original Guildbooks after all. Grouping them into larger books a la The Player's Guide to the High Clans and The Player's Guide to the Low Clans may be a good way to proceed. Added information, more playability, two useful tomes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-05T12:53:14-08:00","id":23910,"title":"","content":"I think so too... That's a lot of books to publish.<br /> <br /> It would make sense to divide them into four categories...<br /> <br /> The Great Guilds:Artificers, Masquers, Pardoners and <i>Usurers</i><br /> The Working Guilds: <i>Chanteurs</i>, <i>Harbingers</i>, Oracles and Sandmen<br /> The Criminal Guilds: Haunters, <i>Monitors</i>, <i>Proctors</i>, Puppeteers and Spooks<br /> The Forbidden Guilds: <i>Alchemists</i>, <i>Solicitors</i> and Mnemoi<br /> <br /> This would be a sensible way to release the books, I think. Each of the books would have previously unreleased content (italicized.) It would probably make sense to start with the Great Guilds, as their arcanoi are so important to the function of wraith society, and work their way down to the underbelly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1078,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","user":"Froggy711","date":". 12-05-2013, 03:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T16:39:26-08:00","id":24738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggy711</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/22091-new-guildbooks-thoughts?p=23910#post23910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think so too... That's a lot of books to publish.<br /> <br /> It would make sense to divide them into four categories...<br /> <br /> The Great Guilds:Artificers, Masquers, Pardoners and <i>Usurers</i><br /> The Working Guilds: <i>Chanteurs</i>, <i>Harbingers</i>, Oracles and Sandmen<br /> The Criminal Guilds: Haunters, <i>Monitors</i>, <i>Proctors</i>, Puppeteers and Spooks<br /> The Forbidden Guilds: <i>Alchemists</i>, <i>Solicitors</i> and Mnemoi<br /> <br /> This would be a sensible way to release the books, I think. Each of the books would have previously unreleased content (italicized.) It would probably make sense to start with the Great Guilds, as their arcanoi are so important to the function of wraith society, and work their way down to the underbelly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like your idea. I really would love to see this as a stretch goal for Wr20","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-07T11:42:21-08:00","id":25267,"title":"","content":"Agreed. I'd also love to see the foreign &quot;Guilds&quot; like the Tvashtriya, Moriman, and so forth get their own books, even if it meant splitting it between them and their respective Dark Kingdoms (so Tvashtriya and Swar, Moriman and The Bush of Ghosts, etc).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1449-zakariya-ali-sher","name":"Zakariya Ali Sher","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T04:59:52-08:00","id":27902,"title":"","content":"I would love it if they just did a new batch of guildbooks instead! I would also love some more dark Kingdom books! I want some Foreign Arcanoi!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 